WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.769
LOGAN ROY:
<i> Let's finish the fucking job
 before this breaks.</i>

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:05.305
Shiv, let's get you out here.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.574
<i>-I need your help on the optics.</i>
-No.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.276
I am not flying out to Argestes
to be the face of this.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.246
Then what the fuck are you doing
on the phone, Siobhan?

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:16.716
♪ (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:17.917 line:0%
This episode is set
in Argestes,

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.686 line:0%
which is like a media
and money conference,

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.890
and there's just deals, deals,
deals, deals everywhere.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.392
Might have just touched
Bill Gates.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.694
JESSE ARMSTRONG:
<i>And all these massive mega deals</i>

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.664
<i> happen in these kind
 of weird ski lodges.</i>

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:32.865
So we always felt it would be

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:34.467
an interesting place
to set an episode.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.371
Maybe we shouldn't
go with "ATN: We're Listening."

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.171
Oh, okay.

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.307
ARMSTRONG:<i> Seeing Tom and Greg
 down by the waterfall</i>

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:44.176
<i> and outside the movie theater
 as they discuss</i>

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.379
this unfortunate information
they find out about

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.615
what the company EPG
has been doing.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.184
There's a grey area
in terms of our data collection,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.720
so that we are kind of like--
We actually are listening.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.689
You know I come from
a comedy-writing background

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.558
and there's something
very comfortable for me

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:02.595
about seeing two very able
comic performers do a bit.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.997
-We're listening?
-Yeah.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.832
But it's just to like maximize
the user experience.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.534
But if that was to break,
maybe--

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.602
Oh, fuck!

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:11.037
The Roys are here.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.839
Permission
to never fucking board?

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.140
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.076
When a scandal hits,
you quickly take on

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.846
<i> a different set of values
 and a different perspective</i>

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.282
which is able
to distance yourself

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.850
from the misdeeds itself.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.853
It's cultural splash back.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.322
We're being punished
for the sins of others.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.691
Logan himself,
in the teeth of a proxy battle,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.260
everyone has that straw
that breaks the camel's back...

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.728
You tortured the old dinosaur.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:36.596
The tipping point.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.497
ROMAN ROY:
You barbecued him live.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.400
It's not like the most violent
attack in the world,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.602
but there's something about
the suddenness and the ferocity,

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.636
<i> and the surprise--</i>

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.605
and I guess that
it's misdirected, you might say.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.641
He was angry, not with Roman,
but with Shiv.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.677
<i>And the fact that Roman gets it
 might be</i>

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.812
<i> an interesting observation
 about the way anger</i>

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.481
and frustration rebounds around
inside a family.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.017
It's a tempest in a tea kettle.
Relax.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.551
I drink them by the pint.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:00.719
It's over.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.722
LOGAN: Hey, hey,
I haven't finished!

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.124
ARMSTRONG:
<i> I think in that moment,
 you see Logan's fear.</i>

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.693
At a certain point,
people walk away,

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:10.229
and that point, I guess,
is what's intriguing to us.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:11.831
What is too much?

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.500
<i> 'Cause the world is tough
 and the world is grubby,</i>

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.302
and you end up having
to bend yourself

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.538
to people around you.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.175
When do you decide
that you're bending too far,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.076
and you're starting to corrupt
something inside?

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:25.745
It's an interesting question.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.816 line:0%
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

